    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="faa4e2c4-6a8a-5734-8bc2-f03b36d5e20d" activityNameId="13c2ebad-ef4c-5c24-a695-4492d651fb4f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Connector, PCI bus, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Connector, PCI bus, at plant
The data represent a current PCI bus type connector like used in current information and communication technology (i.e. computers). Material data are taken from product sheets of producers. The energy demand is estimated based on literature. Infrastructure and transport efforts rough estimations. The dataset represents 1 kg of PCI bus type connectors with a weight of 11.6 gram/unit. In 2023 updates, only production efforts are modified to reflect improved energy efficiency in the manufacturing; UUID: 45d53e81-d92c-3df7-9d1a-017baa1f5d29
This dataset covers raw material input, energy consumption, infrastructure and transport efforts for the production of PCI bus type connectors.
Location: Data represent a global valuable composition of a 64-bit PCI slot connector.
Technology: average connector production technology, based on literature and assumptions
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 
Sampling: literature
Extrapolations: see Geography &amp; Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_45d53e81-d92c-3df7-9d1a-017baa1f5d29.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
